1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,712
This video shows you how to review the change you built,

2
00:00:05,712 --> 00:00:08,350
deploy it, and see records arrive.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,435
Nothing you saved runs until it's deployed.

4
00:00:11,435 --> 00:00:14,590
In the branch bar, open it for review.

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:18,959
smeltr fills in the title and description from what changed.

6
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:22,358
Open it for review.

7
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:26,052
Read through what you're about to deploy.

8
00:00:26,052 --> 00:00:29,518
Every object is added, and none is changed.

9
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:39,390
Your branch is current with main, so main has not changed since you started.

10
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:41,559
Approve and deploy it.

11
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:51,082
smeltr opens Status.

12
00:00:51,082 --> 00:00:54,180
Both workers run the new commit.

13
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:59,257
Back in the terminal, send a fresh record.

14
00:00:59,257 --> 00:01:02,550
Its timestamp tells it apart from earlier ones.

15
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,407
Read the output topic into a file.

16
00:01:05,407 --> 00:01:10,750
The command stops after thirty seconds without another record.

17
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:12,657
Then open it.

18
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:18,330
There's yours: uppercase, with event.dataset added.

19
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:24,510
The three you sent first are there too, because this source starts at the earliest record.

20
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:28,507
Map shows your route, running on the standalone group.

21
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:33,195
Check on learning.

22
00:01:33,395 --> 00:01:35,666
Your change was open for review.

23
00:01:35,666 --> 00:01:38,395
What made your workers run it?

24
00:01:42,795 --> 00:01:44,967
Approving and deploying it.

25
00:01:44,967 --> 00:01:49,188
Deploying changes main, and workers run main.

26
00:01:50,088 --> 00:01:51,644
You sent one record.

27
00:01:51,644 --> 00:01:55,044
Why does the output topic hold four?

28
00:01:59,444 --> 00:02:05,359
Your source starts at the earliest record, so it also read the three you sent first.

29
00:02:06,259 --> 00:02:07,741
That's Getting started.

30
00:02:07,741 --> 00:02:13,175
You installed smeltr, enrolled a worker, built a pipeline, and deployed it.
